Integrating Human In the Loop 

Status: Superseded by ADR-0021

Context:
- AI cannot automate all Workflows.
- Humans can't just review code.

Decision:
- Workflow lifecycle must center around human (user) acceleration.
  Users must be able to halt AI, execute into a running Step, and 
  make modifications to the work done by an Agent. HITL gates
  will still exist and be be specified in Step definitions.
- HITL will occur through ephemeral collaboration. We will inject
  an ephemeral container containing the necessary tools for 

Consequences:
- Workflows will not be automated upfront.
- Ephemeral credentials must be generated for user to safely exec into 
  running Steps.
- Proper tooling must be provided at each Step so a user could accomplish
  the work while the AI acts as the assistant, being given only the 
  necessary context.
- Ephemeral containers expose a larger attack surface, we must implement
  additional malicious detection and prevention methods.

Notes: 
- Superseded 5/21/26: Human in the loop should not be an ephemeral operation. It must be a core part of a Step, and should be natively owned in a separate pod. Advantages/Disadvantages discussed in ADR-0021